WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.152 --> 00:00:06.114
Ben spent the next few days working harder than he'd ever worked before.

2
00:00:27.848 --> 00:00:33.249
On the day before the dress rehearsal, he was backstage with Winnie while she put finishing touches on

3
00:00:33.289 --> 00:00:34.690
the witches' black cauldron.

4
00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:39.251
"The cauldron looks amazing, Winnie," Ben said.

5
00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:42.012
"So do all the costumes."

6
00:00:44.232 --> 00:00:48.133
"Thanks. You were great during your last run-through," Winnie said.

7
00:00:48.153 --> 00:00:50.754
"Are you ready for the dress rehearsal?"

8
00:00:50.774 --> 00:00:53.235
"I think so," Ben replied.

9
00:00:53.255 --> 00:00:57.276
"I finally memorized my lines—without any help from Waldo."

10
00:00:57.856 --> 00:00:58.576
He laughed.

11
00:00:58.596 --> 00:01:02.679
"Uncle Bert told me to sleep with the script under my pillow.

12
00:01:03.999 --> 00:01:06.821
Apparently, that's what lots of Hollyweird actors do."

13
00:01:06.841 --> 00:01:09.622
"Whatever works," Winnie said.

14
00:01:09.642 --> 00:01:12.144
"Are you still worried about the curse?"

15
00:01:12.444 --> 00:01:13.224
Ben asked.

16
00:01:14.205 --> 00:01:14.945
She shrugged.

17
00:01:14.965 --> 00:01:16.326
"Not really.

18
00:01:16.686 --> 00:01:18.907
The show seems to be running smoothly now."

19
00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:20.608
Ben nodded.

20
00:01:21.469 --> 00:01:23.470
"Mog has finally stopped saying that name.

21
00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:27.232
And now that Jen has a headset, she doesn't have to move around so much.

22
00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:30.889
She's not leaving slime trails on the stage anymore."

23
00:01:31.910 --> 00:01:32.830
Winnie chuckled.

24
00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:38.392
"I'd better get the costumes onstage so everyone can see them before rehearsal starts."

25
00:01:40.873 --> 00:01:44.134
Winnie started to roll a large rack filled with costumes.

26
00:01:44.154 --> 00:01:45.915
"Want me to bring the cauldron?"

27
00:01:46.115 --> 00:01:46.856
Ben asked.

28
00:01:46.876 --> 00:01:49.297
"I'll get it later," Winnie said.

29
00:01:53.398 --> 00:01:57.280
A group of excited monsters immediately gathered around the costumes.

30
00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:02.602
"Ooh!" A purple monster pointed to a long white gown.

31
00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.262
"Look at that one!"

32
00:02:04.282 --> 00:02:08.504
"That's for Gaby," a skeleton said.

33
00:02:09.224 --> 00:02:11.165
Ozzy held up a soldier costume.

34
00:02:11.185 --> 00:02:12.766
"I can't wear this.

35
00:02:12.926 --> 00:02:14.106
It doesn't have arms!"

36
00:02:14.126 --> 00:02:17.368
"I'll take that, thank you."

37
00:02:17.788 --> 00:02:21.069
A long serpent monster snatched the costume with his fangs.

38
00:02:21.749 --> 00:02:22.790
He turned to Winnie.

39
00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.191
"This looks fabulous!"

40
00:02:26.872 --> 00:02:27.732
Winnie beamed.

41
00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.488
"I'm glad you like it, Miles."

42
00:02:30.329 --> 00:02:31.449
"Step aside!"

43
00:02:31.789 --> 00:02:34.830
Jade pushed through the crowd, along with the other two witches.

44
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:38.311
"Where are our costumes?"

45
00:02:38.811 --> 00:02:39.631
Sonia asked.

46
00:02:41.212 --> 00:02:43.312
Winnie pulled three costumes off the rack.

47
00:02:44.053 --> 00:02:48.474
The long, dark gowns were covered with cobwebs and intricate beadwork spiders.

48
00:02:50.575 --> 00:02:52.235
Winnie drew in a nervous breath.

49
00:02:52.255 --> 00:02:55.216
"What do you think, witches?"

50
00:02:56.208 --> 00:02:58.110
Sonia was the first witch to speak.

51
00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.812
"We are going to look so good!"

52
00:03:00.832 --> 00:03:03.274
"I love the spiders!"

53
00:03:03.694 --> 00:03:04.495
Jade exclaimed.

54
00:03:05.176 --> 00:03:05.956
Ben grinned.

55
00:03:05.976 --> 00:03:08.278
"Your costumes are a hit, Winnie!"

56
00:03:08.719 --> 00:03:09.379
he whispered.

57
00:03:09.399 --> 00:03:11.201
"Can we try them on?"

58
00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:12.402
Lucy asked.

59
00:03:12.422 --> 00:03:14.603
"I think we should wait for Ms.

60
00:03:14.644 --> 00:03:16.225
Lafang," Winnie said.

61
00:03:16.245 --> 00:03:19.127
"Fine." Lucy tossed her hair.

62
00:03:19.147 --> 00:03:20.829
"What about our cauldron?

63
00:03:21.089 --> 00:03:21.990
Can we see that?"

64
00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.452
"Sure," Winnie said.

65
00:03:24.928 --> 00:03:26.669
"I'll go get it," Ben volunteered.

66
00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:31.152
Ben hurried backstage to retrieve the large papier-mâché cauldron.

67
00:03:31.653 --> 00:03:34.995
But as he bent to pick it up, a light flashed from onstage.

68
00:03:35.015 --> 00:03:37.597
"That was weird," he thought.

69
00:03:38.657 --> 00:03:41.820
As Ben headed back toward the others, the light flashed again.

70
00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.481
Then he saw what had caused it.

71
00:03:44.942 --> 00:03:51.626
While Winnie helped the octopus monster into her costume, the witches were admiring themselves in a handheld mirror.

72
00:03:56.017 --> 00:03:56.977
"No mirrors!"

73
00:03:57.417 --> 00:03:58.138
Ben cried.

74
00:03:58.478 --> 00:04:04.221
He zipped across the stage toward the mirror, without stopping to think—or see the two skeletons in his

75
00:04:04.321 --> 00:04:05.461
way. Boom!

76
00:04:05.922 --> 00:04:10.104
Ben crashed into the two skeletons, sending them clattering to the ground.

77
00:04:10.124 --> 00:04:16.507
He struggled to hold onto the big cauldron, but it slipped from his hands and rolled right into

78
00:04:16.527 --> 00:04:17.667
the rack of costumes.

79
00:04:19.748 --> 00:04:25.252
"Ahh!" Winnie shrieked as the rack went rolling into a stack of open paint cans at the other

80
00:04:25.292 --> 00:04:26.293
side of the stage.

81
00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:31.976
Everyone watched in disbelief as the paint cans flew through the air.

82
00:04:31.996 --> 00:04:36.519
"No!" A big blue monster got hit with green paint.

83
00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.541
A ghoul became pink.

84
00:04:39.822 --> 00:04:46.046
And the cauldron—along with every costume on the rack—was covered in Ben gasped.

85
00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.768
"Bright blue paint!

86
00:04:49.908 --> 00:04:53.351
Remember the superstition—we can't have blue costumes!"

87
00:04:53.371 --> 00:04:56.133
"Our beautiful costumes!"

88
00:04:56.614 --> 00:04:57.415
Sonia cried.

89
00:04:57.435 --> 00:05:01.758
"Ben!" Lucy balled her fists and glowered at him.

90
00:05:01.778 --> 00:05:05.481
"You ruined everything again!"

91
00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:07.243
"I'm sorry!"

92
00:05:07.263 --> 00:05:08.484
Ben cried.

93
00:05:08.504 --> 00:05:14.029
"But mirrors are bad luck onstage, and—" "Students!"

94
00:05:14.589 --> 00:05:17.732
Mr. Freaky shouted, racing into the auditorium.

95
00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:19.541
"What's going on?"

96
00:05:20.161 --> 00:05:25.063
Abruptly he halted, his noses wiggling as he stared in shock at the damage.

97
00:05:30.785 --> 00:05:31.786
did this?"

98
00:05:32.566 --> 00:05:35.247
The witches and a few others spun toward Ben.

99
00:05:35.267 --> 00:05:36.708
"Ben did it!"

100
00:05:37.128 --> 00:05:37.948
Lucy snapped.

101
00:05:38.749 --> 00:05:43.771
"Mirrors and blue costumes might be bad luck onstage—but he's even worse!"

102
00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:46.772
Heat flooded Ben's face.

103
00:05:47.432 --> 00:05:48.433
"It's true, Mr.

104
00:05:48.473 --> 00:05:50.995
Freaky. I was worried about the mirror.

105
00:05:51.435 --> 00:05:57.079
I just wanted to get it offstage before something terrible Ben tried to keep defending himself, but then

106
00:05:57.119 --> 00:05:59.580
he saw the tears streaming down Winnie's face.

107
00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:06.285
He snapped his mouth closed.

108
00:06:06.825 --> 00:06:11.689
Her beautiful costumes and cauldron were ruined, and it was all his fault.

109
00:06:14.450 --> 00:06:17.144
While everyone shouted and yelled, Mr.

110
00:06:17.224 --> 00:06:19.926
Freaky buried his face in his hands and moaned.

111
00:06:25.349 --> 00:06:28.770
Ben floated backstage and slipped out through a back wall.

112
00:06:28.790 --> 00:06:33.273
"I don't know if the curse is real or not," he thought.

113
00:06:33.293 --> 00:06:36.034
"But I don't belong anywhere near a stage.

114
00:06:36.454 --> 00:06:39.576
I'm going to find a hole to crawl into—and never come out!"
